debate in Pennsylvania’s 10th Congressional District race", "source": "ABC27", "published": "2026-09-02T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 4.53, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 3.0, "poll_sd": 8.13, "poll_weight": 0.28, "fundamentals": {"margin": 3.33, "lean": -3.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": 0.13}, "rating_margin": 5.33, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.83, "baseline_margin": 4.1, "analyst_adjustment": 0.1, "key_factors": ["Stelson leads in polling and holds a clear cash-on-hand advantage", "A favorable Democratic climate offsets the district's Republican lean", "Markets and most raters tilt Democratic, though several call it a Tossup", "Perry's incumbency keeps the race genuinely competitive"], "rationale": "The independent Franklin & Marshall poll shows Stelson up three, earlier surveys point the same way, prediction markets price her near 80 percent, and she has out-raised the incumbent with more cash banked. The district's three-point Republican lean and Perry's incumbency argue for caution, but the weight of evidence favors a narrow Democratic edge.", "watch": "A late wave of Republican outside spending or a shift in the economy-focused campaign could erase Stelson's slim lead.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Scott Perry (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's 10th District pairs a Republican-leaning footprint with a strong Democratic national climate, producing one of the cycle's closest House contests. Incumbent Scott Perry faces challenger Janelle Stelson, a former local news anchor who has out-raised him and enters the fall with a sizable cash advantage.\n\nA September Franklin & Marshall poll put Stelson ahead 47 to 44, and earlier surveys, mostly from Democratic sponsors, showed similar margins. Prediction markets price her win odds around 80 percent, while raters split between Tossup calls and Democratic-leaning ratings, with a few going further. The economy tops voters' concerns, and Governor Shapiro's double-digit statewide standing adds favorable terrain. Still, the district's three-point Republican lean and Perry's incumbency keep this genuinely competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7265, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7615, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7786, "margin": 4.2}]}